.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-trust 1  "trust 0.7.2" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-trust \- Manage the trust store (pinned peers)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh trust\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-punch\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-iroh\fR] [\fB\-\-rendezvous\fR] [\fB\-\-jump\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the trust store (pinned peers)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR
When the ssh bootstrap finds no `qsh` on the remote host (or one too old to answer it), install this machine\*(Aqs release into `~/.local/bin` there without asking (`docs/CLI.md` §7). Works with `\-\-json`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR
Never install or upgrade `qsh` on the remote host, and do not ask; a missing `qsh` ends as `remote_qsh_missing`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-punch\fR
Never start a hole punch on this command\*(Aqs behalf, and send no `PunchRequest` (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0054 decision 19). The route is the direct dial alone. Wins over `[punch].mode`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-iroh\fR
Never take the iroh relay route on this command, whatever the host\*(Aqs pin `routes` and `[iroh].mode` say, and contact no relay (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0061 decision 1). On `qsh serve` and `qsh listen` it also keeps the iroh endpoint down, which they otherwise bring up unless `[iroh].enable = false` (ADR\-0063). Not stored
.TP
\fB\-\-rendezvous\fR \fI<PEER>\fR
Use this pinned peer as the rendezvous for hole punching on this command, instead of the host\*(Aqs own `rendezvous` hints (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0054 decision 4). Must be pinned with an address. Not stored
.TP
\fB\-\-jump\fR \fI<HOPS>\fR
Reach the host through these pinned peers, first hop first, for this command: `a` or `a,b` (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0056 decision 20). Each hop is the name of a pin; a `user@` or `:port` on it is ignored by the QUIC path. `none` goes the ordinary way even when the host\*(Aqs pin has a `jump`. Wins over `\-o ProxyJump` and over the pin\*(Aqs own `jump`. Not stored. The short `\-J` is the same flag on the commands that take it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
qsh\-trust\-add(1)
Pin a peer by name
.TP
qsh\-trust\-add\-ca(1)
Register a foreign CA root supplied as a certificate file (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0013). Append\-only: an existing name under a different certificate is refused rather than overwritten
.TP
qsh\-trust\-list(1)
List pinned peers
.TP
qsh\-trust\-remove(1)
Remove a pinned peer. Idempotent
.TP
qsh\-trust\-rename(1)
Rename a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11). Takes effect at the next handshake with no restart required. `acl.toml` is not reloaded: until `qsh serve`/`qsh listen` restarts with a row for the new name, the renamed peer matches no row and is denied (default\-deny); rows naming the old principal no longer apply to it
.TP
qsh\-trust\-set\-role(1)
Change the trust role of a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0045). The only command that changes the role of a pin that already exists. Takes effect from the peer\*(Aqs next request with no restart: roles are read on every decision, unlike `acl.toml` rows. The role is one of `full`, `exec`, `tunnel`, `read\-only`, `reverse`, `none`
.TP
qsh\-trust\-rendezvous(1)
Set which pinned peers are asked to relay a hole punch to a pinned host (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0054 decision 5), most preferred first. Each must be pinned with an address; at most four. The list is also filled in by itself after a connection to the host. `\-\-clear` empties it. Takes effect from the next command
.TP
qsh\-trust\-jump(1)
Set the chain of pinned peers a host is reached through (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0056 decision 20). A dial to the host goes through these hops, first hop first, unless the command line gives `\-J` or `\-\-jump`. Each hop must be pinned with an address; at most four hops, counting the hops\*(Aq own chains, and a name only once. `\-\-clear` removes the chain. Takes effect from the next command
.TP
qsh\-trust\-iroh(1)
Turn the iroh relay route on or off for a pinned host (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0061 decisions 1 and 11). The host is then also tried over an iroh relay when the direct dial and the punch have not stood within `[iroh].head_start_ms`, or at once when the pin has no address. It needs the host\*(Aqs Ed25519 public key (`\-\-key`, 64 hex characters, whose SPKI SHA\-256 must be the pin\*(Aqs fingerprint). `\-\-relay` names the one relay the host is homed on (`https://...`), so the pin has no relay failover; without it every relay of `[iroh].relay_url` is offered and the host may be on any of them. `\-\-off` removes the route; the key stays. Takes effect from the next command. A private CA root cannot take this route
.TP
qsh\-trust\-allow(1)
Grant a pinned peer actions beyond its role (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0051 결정 12). Writes `grants` (and `paths`, `scope`) on the pin in `trust.toml`; takes effect from the peer\*(Aqs next request with no restart. The decision order is the always\-deny gate, the role, these grants, then `acl.toml` rows. Actions are names from the ACL vocabulary or a trailing `.*` family (`forward.*`); `forward.socks` can never be granted. `file.read` and `file.write` need `\-\-path`. A grant only counts for the pin path and for the fingerprint the pin holds now: CA\-authenticated peers and a re\-pinned name do not use it
.TP
qsh\-trust\-deny(1)
Withdraw actions granted with `qsh trust allow` (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0051 결정 12). A running serve notices within a poll tick and closes the pin\*(Aqs established connections that lost an action (ADR\-0031). Does not touch the role: use `qsh trust set\-role` for it
.TP
qsh\-trust\-ssh\-preview(1)
Preview the pins and `[[acl]]` rows an OpenSSH `authorized_keys` file would need (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0026). Read\-only: nothing is pinned and neither `trust.toml` nor `acl.toml` is written
.SH VERSION
v0.7.2
